# Tests of the `slots` module; generated from tools/slots.dsl by tools/build.py. They run under
# `refined test`, where machine and system targets work in the JIT's own process.

# Tests build a shape and a call's slots in the last 4 KiB of machine.state: the shape from byte 61440, the
# arguments from 61952, the results from 62016, the payload at 62080.
slotsTest is test
slotsTest purpose "A shape places each parameter's slots, which read back as numbers, addresses, and flags; text goes into a region; an error stores its payload"
slotsTest verifies slotOf findsSlot
slotsTest verifies argOf readsNumber
slotsTest verifies addressArg readsAddress
slotsTest verifies countOf countsSlots
slotsTest verifies shapeField readsShape
slotsTest verifies flagArg readsFlag
slotsTest verifies putText copiesText
slotsTest verifies failWith storesPayload
slotsTest typeParameter none
slotsTest input none
slotsTest output none
slotsTest outputOwnedBy none
slotsTest raises none
slotsTest effect use machine.memory
slotsTest effect use system.calls
slotsTest uses memoryAccess
slotsTest uses systemCalls
slotsTest memoryHeap false
slotsTest async false
slotsTest maxRecursion none
slotsTest label begin loopKind none
slotsTest label begin within none
slotsTest let label String "slots test" immutable
slotsTest let word String "word" immutable
slotsTest let shapeAt Int64 61440 immutable
slotsTest let argsAt Int64 61952 immutable
slotsTest let resultsAt Int64 62016 immutable
slotsTest let payloadAt Int64 62080 immutable
